menu "ZHAC zhc_adapter"

config ZHAC_METER_POLL_S
    int "Meter poll interval (s), 0 = off"
    default 60
    range 0 86400
    help
      Devices whose definition sets meter_poll (e.g. Tuya TS011F plugs that
      never report power/energy) get their electrical measurement and/or
      metering read every this many seconds, like zigbee2mqtt's
      measurement_poll_interval (default 60). Mains-powered devices only.
      0 turns polling off.

config ZHAC_PING_S
    int "Ping quiet mains devices after (s), 0 = off"
    default 600
    range 0 86400
    help
      A mains-powered device (or one that keeps its receiver on) the hub has
      not heard from for this many seconds gets a ping, a read of Basic
      zclVersion, like zigbee2mqtt's availability (active timeout, default
      10 min). A device that answers keeps a fresh last_seen even when it
      never reports, e.g. a light driven only by its own remote. Unanswered
      pings back off as z2m's do: 1.5x, then twice as long each time, up to
      a day. 0 turns pings off.

endmenu
